  "comment": "No source is published; the maker's manual describes one voice by pointing at the Overon page. The channel count is taken from the widest of sixteen jacks — the main CV and gate, and each voice's two oscillator CV inputs, filter CV input, two envelope gate inputs and own CV and gate inputs — clamped to sixteen and at least one. Every input is scaled by 0.1 on the way into the DSP and every output by 10 on the way out. The two voices are identical, so each control kind carries one line that both voices' tags point at. The coarse tuning range of two octaves either way is the maker's manual; the 440Hz reference is the maker's own."
